{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539590962,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e51523002xItMg3nSXsxxOl","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2e5072b001GVhiqG8llFjrJk","type":"tool","id":"call_351c855d6cc34fa28bc6d5e7","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md, lines 1-182\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Command Surfacing After Phases 005-008 — UX, Performance and Cross-CLI Research Synthesis\"\n3: trigger_phrases: []\n4: ---\n5: # Command Surfacing After Phases 005-008 — UX, Performance and Cross-CLI Research Synthesis\n6: \n7: Merged synthesis of a three-lineage fan-out (`ux`, `performance`, `cross-cli`), 13 iterations in total, executor `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max`. Each lineage's own synthesis stays in `lineages/<label>/research.md`; this file merges, deduplicates and ranks them. Claims the orchestrator re-checked against source are marked `[CHECKED]`.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Executive Summary\n10: \n11: Phases 005-008 build the right thing: the brief is the only surface that can offer a command, and those phases put the command, its policy and its runtime pointer into it. What they leave open is **reachability, attribution and first-run behaviour**, not brief wording or steady-state cost.\n12: \n13: 1. **Two runtimes cannot receive the brief on a normal install.** Codex runs a project hook only after per-entry approval (`trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`), documented in `.codex/README.md` but never in `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`; Codex's 0 of 12 in the before arm had no brief behind it (0 of 6 raw transcripts contain `Advisor:`). DSH's prompt advisor runs only when `promptAdvisor === true`, and `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` never mentions DSH. `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:75]\n14: 2. **The before/after start rate cannot be attributed.** No artifact records that a command was offered, so \"declined\" and \"never offered\" are one number; capped runs sit in the denominator; a `COMMAND:` line appears with the advisor off; and argued routes such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never score a document read. Without an `offered` field the 007 delta is not evidence.\n15: 3. **The first prompt after install is the fragile one.** The embedder cascade probe defaults to 2,500 ms and the CLI waits up to 5,000 ms for a cold daemon, while the Claude shim kills its child at 2,500 ms inside a 3 s host timeout; a cold start between those bounds fails open and the person sees no brief. `/doctor:setup` reports SKIP for the advisor leg exactly when the daemon is cold. `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts:116] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:34] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:20] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:57]\n16: 4. **Steady-state cost is not the constraint.** Hook median 196-205 ms against a 2.5 s budget, a 60-75-token brief, warm embedding 6.57 ms. The token cost that matters is the started command's document (median about 1,131 tokens, p95 about 3,143), not the brief.\n17: \n18: ## 2. Scope, Evidence Lanes, and Terminology\n19: \n20: - **Scope:** improvements after the planned phases 005-008 of `008-command-surfacing-build`; anything those phases already plan is excluded (see §11 cross-check).\n21: - **Lanes:** `ux` (brief content, offer/ask/start, discovery, external install), `performance` (hook time, embedder, cold start, token cost), `cross-cli` (per-runtime start behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh).\n22: - **Terms:** *offered* = the brief named the command; *started* = the scorer's ADR-002 definition (document read, skill load, or `COMMAND: … started`); *capped* = run ended by the harness time cap (exit 143 or null).\n23: - **Rules held:** no holdout corpus rows read, no pi run, no ollama control, no process kill, no full vitest suite, read-only git.\n24: \n25: ## 3. Before-Arm Baseline (rescored at synthesis, 2026-11-12T23:18Z)\n26: \n27: The arm was still growing during the run, so each lineage saw a different snapshot (OpenCode was 3/7, 4/9, 5/10 and 5/12 at different moments). This is the single snapshot used here, from `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` (exit 0):\n28: \n29: | Runtime | Rows scored | Start | `COMMAND:` lines | Capped | Unsafe |\n30: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n31: | claude | 24 | 3 of 12 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n32: | codex | 24 | 0 of 12 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n33: | pi | 24 | 0 of 12 | 0 | 2 | 3 |\n34: | devin | 24 | 3 of 12 | 0 | 6 | 3 |\n35: | opencode | 24 | 5 of 12 | 0 | 7 | 2 |\n36: | dsh | 18 | 5 of 12 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n37: \n38: Because phase 005 is unbuilt, no row was offered a command; every start above is a spontaneous document read. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n39: \n40: ## 4. Six-Runtime Delivery Inventory\n41: \n42: | Runtime | Delivery path | Processes per prompt | Brief delivered? | Command surface |\n43: |---|---|---|---|---|\n44: | claude | spec-kit shim → advisor hook → CLI | 3 | yes (6/6 raw transcripts) | folder tree; 32 of 44 visible (G5) |\n45: | codex | adapter → advisor hook → CLI | 3 | **no** in the arena (hooks unapproved) | flat prompts (`create-readme`) |\n46: | devin | adapter → advisor hook → CLI | 3 | wired; not observable in records | none (skills only) |\n47: | pi | in-process extension → CLI | 2 | yes, in-prompt (6/6) | flat prompts |\n48: | opencode | in-process plugin → CLI | 2 | wired; 1 of 6 sessions shows it | folder tree; same `skill.md` risk, untested |\n49: | dsh | in-process plugin → CLI, behind `promptAdvisor` | 2 | **off by default** | flat prompts |\n50: \n51: [SOURCE: lineages/cross-cli/research.md §4.4] [SOURCE: lineages/performance/research.md §7]\n52: \n53: ## 5. Findings — Reachability (cross-cli lane)\n54: \n55: 1. Codex hook approval is a product step that the install path omits. `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:75]\n56: 2. DSH is off by default and absent from the install guide (`grep -ci dsh INSTALL-SKILLED.md` = 0). `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53]\n57: 3. A target repo that already has `.claude/settings.json` (or a codex/cursor/devin hook file) keeps it through the doctor merge and never receives the `UserPromptSubmit` entry; no setup leg checks it. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs:821]\n58: 4. Host command names differ from canonical: `/create:readme` on Claude and OpenCode, `create-readme` on Codex, Pi, DSH and Cursor, no command surface on Devin. The brief carries only the canonical form. [SOURCE: .codex/prompts/create-readme.md:2] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:202]\n59: 5. G5: `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` is the only lowercase `skill.md` command file; its Claude mirror hides 12 sibling `create:*` commands (Claude exposes 32 of 44). The G5 listing used a stand-in folder, and OpenCode's behaviour on the same mirror is untested. `[CHECKED: file present]` [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n60: 6. `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions` already carries `runtime`, so a per-runtime head is a change inside `renderAdvisorBrief`, not a new data flow. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:48]\n61: 7. Pi is the only runtime whose brief is observable inside the prompt, which makes it the clean A/B bed for head changes.\n62: \n63: ## 6. Findings — Measurement Integrity (ux and cross-cli lanes)\n64: \n65: 1. The closed diagnostic record holds `skillLabel`, `emittedBytes`, `directivesSuppressed` and no command or policy, so an offer cannot be told apart from a decline. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:50]\n66: 2. Capped runs stay in `startRows`: OpenCode 5 of 12 is at best 5 of 5 uncapped, Devin 3 of 12 at best 3 of 6. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1082]\n67: 3. The aggregate rate hides a policy split that inverts by runtime: Claude starts 3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows; OpenCode and DSH start 3 of 8 mutating rows.\n68: 4. Start rate measures the path, not the outcome: Devin produced `/create:agent` artifacts while scoring `started: false`.\n69: 5. `commandParts('/doctor:git hooks')` looks up `doctor/git hooks.md`; 28 of 35 doctor strings carry an argument and can never score a document read. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\n70: 6. DSH emitted a `COMMAND:` line with its advisor disabled, so the token alone does not prove an offer.\n71: 7. Policy reaches only the command: on `ask` rows with no offer, Devin created a council scratch folder and Pi wrote a fixture without asking. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\n72: \n73: ## 7. Findings — Performance and Cost (performance lane)\n74: \n75: | Item | Measured | Source |\n76: |---|---|---|\n77: | Claude hook median / p95 | 205.09 / 261.92 ms (44 prompts); ux probe 196.2 / 352.4 ms (40) | `004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-after-3.json`; ux iteration 5 |\n78: | Bare `node -e 0` start | 36.85 ms median (n=15) | performance lineage, local |\n79: | Advisor CLI warm | 62.7-71.3 ms | `008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:18` |\n80: | Warm / cold query embed | 6.57 ms / 271-277 ms | same file :12; `008.../spec.md:130` |\n81: | Model unload | 5-minute default; no `keep_alive` sent `[CHECKED]` | `shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts` |\n82: | Brief | 242-298 bytes, 60-75 tokens; 233 bytes is the constant directive | `runtime/lib/render.ts:162` |\n83: | Command documents (44) | median 4,524 B (~1,131 t), p95 12,573 B (~3,143 t) | `git ls-files` + stat |\n84: \n85: 1. About 100-110 ms of the Claude median is three Node process starts; the adapter spawn and the CLI spawn are each removable (estimated Claude 205 → ~131 ms).\n86: 2. Cold-start bounds are inverted on Claude and Codex: cascade probe 2,500 ms and CLI cold wait 5,000 ms against a 2,500 ms shim kill (Claude) and a 2,800 ms adapter budget (Codex). Devin and Cursor pass 10 s and are safe. A sandbox record already shows a 2,508 ms fail-open.\n87: 3. The embedder cold tax (271-277 ms) fits phase 008's planned 750 ms deadline, so it is latency, not failure; but `getAdapter(name)` takes no options, so a wrapper race would abandon a live 5 s request instead of aborting it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts:83]\n88: 4. Hook health (rolling p95, fail-open rate) is computed but only `advisor_validate` returns it; `advisor_status` and `/doctor:setup` do not. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-validate.ts:624]\n89: 5. Performance does not explain the start-rate spread: hook cost is the same order on every runtime.\n90: \n91: ## 8. Cross-Lineage Agreement and Conflict\n92: \n93: - **Agree:** attribution fields (ux R2-R4, cross-cli R4); command document path in the head (ux R7, cross-cli R3); G5 needs a real-path test (ux R16, cross-cli R5); cold first prompt is the fragile path (ux R6, performance P1).\n94: - **Conflict 1 — process-chain collapse.** performance P2/P3 recommends in-process adapters and daemon RPC (-36% median). ux eliminates it: p95 uses 16% of budget, the gain is not perceptible and the refactor touches the timeout boundary. This synthesis ranks it low and conditional on a measured cold-start win (§9, rank 13).\n95: - **Conflict 2 — document path scope.** ux puts the path in every head; cross-cli limits it to codex, pi and dsh to save tokens where the host resolves commands itself. This synthesis takes the runtime-conditional form, because the Claude `create:*` case is better solved by the G5 fix, and Pi gives a clean A/B.\n96: - **Tension with phase 008 — `keep_alive`.** performance P4 keeps the embed model loaded; phase 008 keeps it cold by design. Listed as a decision, not a recommendation.\n97: \n98: ## 9. Ranked Recommendations\n99: \n100: Ranked by expected start-rate gain or silent failure removed, per unit of work. Each item names the file, the gain, and the check.\n101: \n102: | # | Recommendation | File(s) | Measurable gain | Verify |\n103: |---|---|---|---|---|\n104: | 1 | Put Codex hook approval in the install path and add a doctor check | `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (step after build), runtime-mirrors doctor route under `.skilled/commands/doctor/`, link from `.codex/README.md` | Codex goes from a structural 0 (no brief) to a measured runtime; up to 12 rows become attributable | One Codex smoke run's rollout contains `Advisor:`; doctor prints `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved` on a fresh clone, `PASS` after approval |\n105: | 2 | Record the offer: `offeredCommand`/`offeredPolicy` in the diagnostic record and each arm run line | `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, `hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Offer rate becomes countable; today 0 rows can say a command was offered; no extra latency | Fixture serializes both fields; each run line carries them |\n106: | 3 | Make the scorer report an attributable rate: `offered X, started Y of X`, capped excluded, `arm incomplete`, per-policy start and `wrote` counts | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | \"3 of 12\" becomes a delta that is evidence; hides no risky-class regression | 23-of-24 fixture prints `arm incomplete`; `--summary --json` shows `byPolicy.start` with `wrote` |\n107: | 4 | Remove the cold-start fail-open: detached `advisor_status --warm-only` at SessionStart, and a cascade probe timeout below the hook budget | `.claude/settings.json` and `.codex/hooks.json` SessionStart; `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` (`SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=750`) | First-prompt fail-open count on Claude and Codex → 0; first prompt bounded by the hook budget | Measure a cold start in a sandbox socket dir first; fresh-session `hook-latency.mjs` shows `fail_open` 0 on first prompts; a hung-stub launch returns inside budget |\n108: | 5 | Make DSH reachable: list it in the install guide and default the prompt advisor on when the row is absent | `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md` | One more runtime that can receive a brief; DSH's 5 of 12 is currently measured with the advisor off | One DSH smoke run's step payload contains `Advisor:`; `grep -ci dsh INSTALL-SKILLED.md` ≥ 2; plugin default test updated |\n109: | 6 | Check the target repo's hook wiring on first run | new `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, called from `/doctor:symlink check --root` | A silent no-brief install becomes `hook-missing <runtime>` with a repair, across 4 native hook configs | Fixture without the entry exits 1 naming `hook-missing claude`; with it exits 0 |\n110: | 7 | Name the command document path in the head on hosts without a folder-style registry | `runtime/lib/render.ts` (`renderAdvisorBrief`, use the existing `runtime` option); golden heads in `ADV/tests` | Removes one inference per start on codex, pi, dsh; head stays under the 140-byte guard (~+40 bytes) | Pi-only A/B over the 12 start rows: `started` rises, `unsafe` unchanged; golden paths resolve with `test -f` |\n111: | 8 | Bind the command's run/ask policy to the skill path that runs the same workflow | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 bullet (extends the 006 text) | Stops `ask`-row writes like the Devin and Pi ones; Pi 3 and Devin 3 unsafe in the before arm | `rg -c \"policy applies to the skill path\" AGENTS.md` = 1; post arm `unsafe 0` per runtime |\n112: | 9 | Settle G5 on the real path and guard it: reproduce with a throwaway `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, also on OpenCode, then add a per-runtime visibility count to `--check` | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` (`--check` counts, one-entry allowlist); `007/scratch/g5/` listings | 12 hidden `create:*` names become visible, or G5 closes as a stand-in artifact; a second `skill.md` cannot ship | Two listings per runtime diff on the 12 names; `--check` prints `claude 32/44` today and exits 1 on a new collision |\n113: | 10 | Fix the argued-route document lookup | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (`commandParts` / `documentTails`) | 28 of 35 doctor strings become scorable; no false decline on doctor rows | `/doctor:git hooks` case reading `doctor/git.md` returns `started: true`; targeted vitest 0 failed |\n114: | 11 | Thread the 750 ms embed deadline into the adapter as a real abort, not a wrapper race | `shared/embeddings/registry.ts:83` (options), `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:128` | Request aborts at 750 ms instead of holding a socket for 5 s; correct `disabledReason` | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` plus an abort-vs-race assertion |\n115: | 12 | Surface hook health and add a \"prove it\" install step | `runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, advisor leg text in `doctor-setup.yaml`; `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` §2 | The person sees `p95 352 ms, 273 bytes` and a pass or named failure instead of SKIP on a cold install | `advisor_status --format json \\| jq .data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms` prints a number; documented command prints a recommendation |\n116: | 13 | (Conditional) Collapse the host-adapter spawn and the CLI spawn | `runtime/hooks/codex/shared.ts` and Devin/Cursor siblings; `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | About 74 ms per Claude prompt (205 → ~131 ms) | Only after rank 4's cold-start measurement shows it matters; hook-latency median ≤ 135 ms, CLI fallback tests pass |\n117: | 14 | Small guards: native-spelling column in the 006 surface table; once-per-command clause unconditional; 44-row head-length matrix; session brief-cost script; command read-cost report flagging `start` docs over 8 KB; machine-readable `write_targets` | `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`; `AGENTS.md`; `ADV/tests`; new `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `measure-command-read-cost.mjs`; `*/command-metadata.json` | Each makes one silent drift visible (5 of 44 docs over 8 KB today; worst head 136 of 140 bytes) | Each script prints its row counts; a 141-byte fixture fails; `repeated 0` in the post arm |\n118: \n119: ## Eliminated Alternatives\n120: \n121: | Approach | Reason Eliminated | Evidence | Iteration(s) |\n122: |---|---|---|---|\n123: | \"Most runtimes have no hook wired\" | Five of six have a live path; Codex and Devin proxy the Claude adapter | Delivery inventory §4 | cross-cli 1 |\n124: | \"Codex declined the offered command\" | Codex received no brief: hooks unapproved, 0 of 6 transcripts with `Advisor:` | `.codex/README.md:54` | cross-cli 1-2 |\n125: | \"The hook is too slow, so the brief is dropped\" | Warm median ~200 ms against 2.5 s; only the cold path fails | `measured-2026-11-12.txt` | cross-cli 1; performance 1-3 |\n126: | \"A `COMMAND:` line proves an offer\" | DSH emitted one with the advisor off | runs-pre.jsonl | cross-cli 2 |\n127: | Trim the comment-hygiene directive to save tokens | Carries a repo hard block; suppressed after the first message; at most 54 tokens per session | `render.ts:162` | ux 1, 5; performance 4 |\n128: | Rename `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` | Blocked by decision Q025; rank 7 and 9 reach the same commands | decision-record | ux 3 |\n129: | Semantic or persisted prompt cache, new vector precompute | Pays an embedding to decide a hit; vectors already exist; no field hit rate measurable | `prompt-cache.ts:16`, `metrics.ts:319` | performance 4 |\n130: | Longer cold timeout | Trades a fast fail-open for a 5 s first-prompt stall | — | performance 3 |\n131: | Show the degraded meaning lane in the brief | Ruled out by decision Q037 | decision-record | ux 4 |\n132: | Add a recommendation leg to `/doctor:setup` | Route invariant forbids starting the daemon; the proof goes in the install guide | `doctor-setup.yaml` | ux 4 |\n133: | Re-run the before arm in research | Phase 007 owns the arm; research may not start CLI runs | steer.md | ux 2 |\n134: | Treat Claude's low rate as a brief failure | Same brief yields 3 of 4 read-only starts and 0 of 8 mutating starts | runs-pre.jsonl | ux 2 |\n135: \n136: ## Divergence Map\n137: \n138: No divergent pivots were taken in any lineage. Saturated directions: directive trimming, the `create` rename, caching and precompute, steady-state latency. Remaining frontier: the post-arm behaviour of the planned head (needs ranks 2-3 first), the cold daemon start time (needs a sandbox socket measurement), OpenCode's folder rule for `skill.md`, Devin's delivery observability, and the Codex and DSH smoke runs.\n139: \n140: ## 12. Open Questions\n141: \n142: 1. Does an offer move mutating starts on Claude and Codex? Only the post arm with ranks 2-3 in place can say.\n143: 2. What does a cold first prompt cost end to end? Unmeasured under this run's rules (no daemon or ollama control); it bounds the gain of ranks 4 and 13.\n144: 3. Does OpenCode collapse a folder that holds `skill.md`?\n145: 4. How does a failed host invocation (a model typing `/create:readme` in Codex) show up? It leaves no tool call and no scored fact today.\n146: 5. Is the Devin brief delivered? The shim is wired; the sampled records cannot show it.\n147: 6. Should the embed model stay warm (`keep_alive`) against phase 008's cold-by-design choice? Operator decision.\n148: \n149: ## 13. References\n150: \n151: - Parent packet `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/`: `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`, `goal.md`; `plan.md` and `tasks.md` of `005`-`008`; `007/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`, `007/scratch/g5/result.txt`; `008/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt`\n152: - Lineage syntheses: `lineages/ux/research.md`, `lineages/performance/research.md`, `lineages/cross-cli/research.md`; iterations under `lineages/<label>/iterations/`\n153: - Merged registry `findings-registry.json` (67 key findings), attribution `fanout-attribution.md`, resource map `resource-map.md`\n154: - Runtime surfaces: `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/README.md`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`\n155: - Advisor code: `runtime/lib/render.ts`, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`; `system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/{auto-select.ts,registry.ts,adapters/ollama.ts}`\n156: \n157: ## 14. Answered Questions\n158: \n159: - What stops a model from starting an offered command, per runtime: Codex and DSH never get the brief on a normal install; elsewhere no offer exists yet (pre-005), and capability judgment splits read-only from mutating commands. Answered.\n160: - Where hook time goes and what removes the fail-open: answered (§7, rank 4).\n161: - Token cost per prompt and per start: answered (brief 60-75 tokens; started document ~1,131 tokens median).\n162: - Discovery defects: answered (G5, three spellings, no visibility check).\n163: - External install path: answered (no Codex approval step, no DSH, existing hook configs win, setup SKIPs cold).\n164: \n165: ## 15. Limitations and Confidence\n166: \n167: - Executor is a flash model; numbers it reports were spot-checked by the orchestrator for the load-bearing items (Codex approval, DSH flag, cascade and cold-start timeouts, no `keep_alive`, `/doctor:setup` SKIP, `skill.md` presence). Others carry the lineage's citation only.\n168: - The before arm grew during the run; §3 is the single snapshot used for ranking.\n169: - Gains for ranks 4, 7 and 13 are estimates until the cold-start and Pi A/B measurements exist.\n170: - The ux lineage ran the real hook 47 times, which appended telemetry rows under `$TMPDIR/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/` (outside the repository).\n171: \n172: ## 16. Implementation Decision\n173: \n174: Recommended next packet: ranks 1-6 as one reachability-and-attribution phase after 007's after arm, because ranks 2-3 are required for that arm to be evidence and ranks 1, 4, 5 and 6 decide whether a brief exists at all on four runtimes. Ranks 7-12 follow once the post arm shows which runtimes still decline. Rank 13 waits on the cold-start measurement. Operator decision needed on `keep_alive` (§12 Q6).\n175: \n176: ## 17. Convergence Report\n177: \n178: - Stop reason: per lineage — `cross-cli` converged after 3 iterations (all 5 questions answered); `performance` reached its 5-iteration cap (last ratio 0.45); `ux` reached its 5-iteration cap (ratios 0.83-0.90).\n179: - Total iterations: 13 (ux 5, performance 5, cross-cli 3)\n180: - Questions answered: cross-cli 5/5, performance 5/5, ux 4/5 substantive (KQ1 half answered: model-side behaviour needs the post arm)\n181: - Convergence threshold: 0.05\n182: - Divergence summary: no divergent pivots recorded","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md, lines 1-182\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Command Surfacing After Phases 005-008 — UX, Performance and Cross-CLI Research Synthesis\"\n3: trigger_phrases: []\n4: ---\n5: # Command Surfacing After Phases 005-008 — UX, Performance and Cross-CLI Research Synthesis\n6: \n7: Merged synthesis of a three-lineage fan-out (`ux`, `performance`, `cross-cli`), 13 iterations in total, executor `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max`. Each lineage's own synthesis stays in `lineages/<label>/research.md`; this file merges, deduplicates and ranks them. Claims the orchestrator re-checked against source are marked `[CHECKED]`.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Executive Summary\n10: \n11: Phases 005-008 build the right thing: the brief is the only surface that can offer a command, and those phases put the command, its policy and its runtime pointer into it. What they leave open is **reachability, attribution and first-run behaviour**, not brief wording or steady-state cost.\n12: \n13: 1. **Two runtimes cannot receive the brief on a normal install.** Codex runs a project hook only after per-entry approval (`trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`), documented in `.codex/README.md` but never in `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`; Codex's 0 of 12 in the before arm had no brief behind it (0 of 6 raw transcripts contain `Advisor:`). DSH's prompt advisor runs only when `promptAdvisor === true`, and `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` never mentions DSH. `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:75]\n14: 2. **The before/after start rate cannot be attributed.** No artifact records that a command was offered, so \"declined\" and \"never offered\" are one number; capped runs sit in the denominator; a `COMMAND:` line appears with the advisor off; and argued routes such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never score a document read. Without an `offered` field the 007 delta is not evidence.\n15: 3. **The first prompt after install is the fragile one.** The embedder cascade probe defaults to 2,500 ms and the CLI waits up to 5,000 ms for a cold daemon, while the Claude shim kills its child at 2,500 ms inside a 3 s host timeout; a cold start between those bounds fails open and the person sees no brief. `/doctor:setup` reports SKIP for the advisor leg exactly when the daemon is cold. `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts:116] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:34] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:20] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:57]\n16: 4. **Steady-state cost is not the constraint.** Hook median 196-205 ms against a 2.5 s budget, a 60-75-token brief, warm embedding 6.57 ms. The token cost that matters is the started command's document (median about 1,131 tokens, p95 about 3,143), not the brief.\n17: \n18: ## 2. Scope, Evidence Lanes, and Terminology\n19: \n20: - **Scope:** improvements after the planned phases 005-008 of `008-command-surfacing-build`; anything those phases already plan is excluded (see §11 cross-check).\n21: - **Lanes:** `ux` (brief content, offer/ask/start, discovery, external install), `performance` (hook time, embedder, cold start, token cost), `cross-cli` (per-runtime start behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh).\n22: - **Terms:** *offered* = the brief named the command; *started* = the scorer's ADR-002 definition (document read, skill load, or `COMMAND: … started`); *capped* = run ended by the harness time cap (exit 143 or null).\n23: - **Rules held:** no holdout corpus rows read, no pi run, no ollama control, no process kill, no full vitest suite, read-only git.\n24: \n25: ## 3. Before-Arm Baseline (rescored at synthesis, 2026-11-12T23:18Z)\n26: \n27: The arm was still growing during the run, so each lineage saw a different snapshot (OpenCode was 3/7, 4/9, 5/10 and 5/12 at different moments). This is the single snapshot used here, from `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` (exit 0):\n28: \n29: | Runtime | Rows scored | Start | `COMMAND:` lines | Capped | Unsafe |\n30: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n31: | claude | 24 | 3 of 12 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n32: | codex | 24 | 0 of 12 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n33: | pi | 24 | 0 of 12 | 0 | 2 | 3 |\n34: | devin | 24 | 3 of 12 | 0 | 6 | 3 |\n35: | opencode | 24 | 5 of 12 | 0 | 7 | 2 |\n36: | dsh | 18 | 5 of 12 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n37: \n38: Because phase 005 is unbuilt, no row was offered a command; every start above is a spontaneous document read. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n39: \n40: ## 4. Six-Runtime Delivery Inventory\n41: \n42: | Runtime | Delivery path | Processes per prompt | Brief delivered? | Command surface |\n43: |---|---|---|---|---|\n44: | claude | spec-kit shim → advisor hook → CLI | 3 | yes (6/6 raw transcripts) | folder tree; 32 of 44 visible (G5) |\n45: | codex | adapter → advisor hook → CLI | 3 | **no** in the arena (hooks unapproved) | flat prompts (`create-readme`) |\n46: | devin | adapter → advisor hook → CLI | 3 | wired; not observable in records | none (skills only) |\n47: | pi | in-process extension → CLI | 2 | yes, in-prompt (6/6) | flat prompts |\n48: | opencode | in-process plugin → CLI | 2 | wired; 1 of 6 sessions shows it | folder tree; same `skill.md` risk, untested |\n49: | dsh | in-process plugin → CLI, behind `promptAdvisor` | 2 | **off by default** | flat prompts |\n50: \n51: [SOURCE: lineages/cross-cli/research.md §4.4] [SOURCE: lineages/performance/research.md §7]\n52: \n53: ## 5. Findings — Reachability (cross-cli lane)\n54: \n55: 1. Codex hook approval is a product step that the install path omits. `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:75]\n56: 2. DSH is off by default and absent from the install guide (`grep -ci dsh INSTALL-SKILLED.md` = 0). `[CHECKED]` [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53]\n57: 3. A target repo that already has `.claude/settings.json` (or a codex/cursor/devin hook file) keeps it through the doctor merge and never receives the `UserPromptSubmit` entry; no setup leg checks it. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs:821]\n58: 4. Host command names differ from canonical: `/create:readme` on Claude and OpenCode, `create-readme` on Codex, Pi, DSH and Cursor, no command surface on Devin. The brief carries only the canonical form. [SOURCE: .codex/prompts/create-readme.md:2] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:202]\n59: 5. G5: `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` is the only lowercase `skill.md` command file; its Claude mirror hides 12 sibling `create:*` commands (Claude exposes 32 of 44). The G5 listing used a stand-in folder, and OpenCode's behaviour on the same mirror is untested. `[CHECKED: file present]` [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n60: 6. `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions` already carries `runtime`, so a per-runtime head is a change inside `renderAdvisorBrief`, not a new data flow. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:48]\n61: 7. Pi is the only runtime whose brief is observable inside the prompt, which makes it the clean A/B bed for head changes.\n62: \n63: ## 6. Findings — Measurement Integrity (ux and cross-cli lanes)\n64: \n65: 1. The closed diagnostic record holds `skillLabel`, `emittedBytes`, `directivesSuppressed` and no command or policy, so an offer cannot be told apart from a decline. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:50]\n66: 2. Capped runs stay in `startRows`: OpenCode 5 of 12 is at best 5 of 5 uncapped, Devin 3 of 12 at best 3 of 6. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1082]\n67: 3. The aggregate rate hides a policy split that inverts by runtime: Claude starts 3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows; OpenCode and DSH start 3 of 8 mutating rows.\n68: 4. Start rate measures the path, not the outcome: Devin produced `/create:agent` artifacts while scoring `started: false`.\n69: 5. `commandParts('/doctor:git hooks')` looks up `doctor/git hooks.md`; 28 of 35 doctor strings carry an argument and can never score a document read. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\n70: 6. DSH emitted a `COMMAND:` line with its advisor disabled, so the token alone does not prove an offer.\n71: 7. Policy reaches only the command: on `ask` rows with no offer, Devin created a council scratch folder and Pi wrote a fixture without asking. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\n72: \n73: ## 7. Findings — Performance and Cost (performance lane)\n74: \n75: | Item | Measured | Source |\n76: |---|---|---|\n77: | Claude hook median / p95 | 205.09 / 261.92 ms (44 prompts); ux probe 196.2 / 352.4 ms (40) | `004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-after-3.json`; ux iteration 5 |\n78: | Bare `node -e 0` start | 36.85 ms median (n=15) | performance lineage, local |\n79: | Advisor CLI warm | 62.7-71.3 ms | `008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:18` |\n80: | Warm / cold query embed | 6.57 ms / 271-277 ms | same file :12; `008.../spec.md:130` |\n81: | Model unload | 5-minute default; no `keep_alive` sent `[CHECKED]` | `shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts` |\n82: | Brief | 242-298 bytes, 60-75 tokens; 233 bytes is the constant directive | `runtime/lib/render.ts:162` |\n83: | Command documents (44) | median 4,524 B (~1,131 t), p95 12,573 B (~3,143 t) | `git ls-files` + stat |\n84: \n85: 1. About 100-110 ms of the Claude median is three Node process starts; the adapter spawn and the CLI spawn are each removable (estimated Claude 205 → ~131 ms).\n86: 2. Cold-start bounds are inverted on Claude and Codex: cascade probe 2,500 ms and CLI cold wait 5,000 ms against a 2,500 ms shim kill (Claude) and a 2,800 ms adapter budget (Codex). Devin and Cursor pass 10 s and are safe. A sandbox record already shows a 2,508 ms fail-open.\n87: 3. The embedder cold tax (271-277 ms) fits phase 008's planned 750 ms deadline, so it is latency, not failure; but `getAdapter(name)` takes no options, so a wrapper race would abandon a live 5 s request instead of aborting it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts:83]\n88: 4. Hook health (rolling p95, fail-open rate) is computed but only `advisor_validate` returns it; `advisor_status` and `/doctor:setup` do not. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-validate.ts:624]\n89: 5. Performance does not explain the start-rate spread: hook cost is the same order on every runtime.\n90: \n91: ## 8. Cross-Lineage Agreement and Conflict\n92: \n93: - **Agree:** attribution fields (ux R2-R4, cross-cli R4); command document path in the head (ux R7, cross-cli R3); G5 needs a real-path test (ux R16, cross-cli R5); cold first prompt is the fragile path (ux R6, performance P1).\n94: - **Conflict 1 — process-chain collapse.** performance P2/P3 recommends in-process adapters and daemon RPC (-36% median). ux eliminates it: p95 uses 16% of budget, the gain is not perceptible and the refactor touches the timeout boundary. This synthesis ranks it low and conditional on a measured cold-start win (§9, rank 13).\n95: - **Conflict 2 — document path scope.** ux puts the path in every head; cross-cli limits it to codex, pi and dsh to save tokens where the host resolves commands itself. This synthesis takes the runtime-conditional form, because the Claude `create:*` case is better solved by the G5 fix, and Pi gives a clean A/B.\n96: - **Tension with phase 008 — `keep_alive`.** performance P4 keeps the embed model loaded; phase 008 keeps it cold by design. Listed as a decision, not a recommendation.\n97: \n98: ## 9. Ranked Recommendations\n99: \n100: Ranked by expected start-rate gain or silent failure removed, per unit of work. Each item names the file, the gain, and the check.\n101: \n102: | # | Recommendation | File(s) | Measurable gain | Verify |\n103: |---|---|---|---|---|\n104: | 1 | Put Codex hook approval in the install path and add a doctor check | `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (step after build), runtime-mirrors doctor route under `.skilled/commands/doctor/`, link from `.codex/README.md` | Codex goes from a structural 0 (no brief) to a measured runtime; up to 12 rows become attributable | One Codex smoke run's rollout contains `Advisor:`; doctor prints `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved` on a fresh clone, `PASS` after approval |\n105: | 2 | Record the offer: `offeredCommand`/`offeredPolicy` in the diagnostic record and each arm run line | `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, `hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Offer rate becomes countable; today 0 rows can say a command was offered; no extra latency | Fixture serializes both fields; each run line carries them |\n106: | 3 | Make the scorer report an attributable rate: `offered X, started Y of X`, capped excluded, `arm incomplete`, per-policy start and `wrote` counts | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | \"3 of 12\" becomes a delta that is evidence; hides no risky-class regression | 23-of-24 fixture prints `arm incomplete`; `--summary --json` shows `byPolicy.start` with `wrote` |\n107: | 4 | Remove the cold-start fail-open: detached `advisor_status --warm-only` at SessionStart, and a cascade probe timeout below the hook budget | `.claude/settings.json` and `.codex/hooks.json` SessionStart; `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` (`SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=750`) | First-prompt fail-open count on Claude and Codex → 0; first prompt bounded by the hook budget | Measure a cold start in a sandbox socket dir first; fresh-session `hook-latency.mjs` shows `fail_open` 0 on first prompts; a hung-stub launch returns inside budget |\n108: | 5 | Make DSH reachable: list it in the install guide and default the prompt advisor on when the row is absent | `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md` | One more runtime that can receive a brief; DSH's 5 of 12 is currently measured with the advisor off | One DSH smoke run's step payload contains `Advisor:`; `grep -ci dsh INSTALL-SKILLED.md` ≥ 2; plugin default test updated |\n109: | 6 | Check the target repo's hook wiring on first run | new `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, called from `/doctor:symlink check --root` | A silent no-brief install becomes `hook-missing <runtime>` with a repair, across 4 native hook configs | Fixture without the entry exits 1 naming `hook-missing claude`; with it exits 0 |\n110: | 7 | Name the command document path in the head on hosts without a folder-style registry | `runtime/lib/render.ts` (`renderAdvisorBrief`, use the existing `runtime` option); golden heads in `ADV/tests` | Removes one inference per start on codex, pi, dsh; head stays under the 140-byte guard (~+40 bytes) | Pi-only A/B over the 12 start rows: `started` rises, `unsafe` unchanged; golden paths resolve with `test -f` |\n111: | 8 | Bind the command's run/ask policy to the skill path that runs the same workflow | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 bullet (extends the 006 text) | Stops `ask`-row writes like the Devin and Pi ones; Pi 3 and Devin 3 unsafe in the before arm | `rg -c \"policy applies to the skill path\" AGENTS.md` = 1; post arm `unsafe 0` per runtime |\n112: | 9 | Settle G5 on the real path and guard it: reproduce with a throwaway `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, also on OpenCode, then add a per-runtime visibility count to `--check` | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` (`--check` counts, one-entry allowlist); `007/scratch/g5/` listings | 12 hidden `create:*` names become visible, or G5 closes as a stand-in artifact; a second `skill.md` cannot ship | Two listings per runtime diff on the 12 names; `--check` prints `claude 32/44` today and exits 1 on a new collision |\n113: | 10 | Fix the argued-route document lookup | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (`commandParts` / `documentTails`) | 28 of 35 doctor strings become scorable; no false decline on doctor rows | `/doctor:git hooks` case reading `doctor/git.md` returns `started: true`; targeted vitest 0 failed |\n114: | 11 | Thread the 750 ms embed deadline into the adapter as a real abort, not a wrapper race | `shared/embeddings/registry.ts:83` (options), `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:128` | Request aborts at 750 ms instead of holding a socket for 5 s; correct `disabledReason` | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` plus an abort-vs-race assertion |\n115: | 12 | Surface hook health and add a \"prove it\" install step | `runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, advisor leg text in `doctor-setup.yaml`; `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` §2 | The person sees `p95 352 ms, 273 bytes` and a pass or named failure instead of SKIP on a cold install | `advisor_status --format json \\| jq .data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms` prints a number; documented command prints a recommendation |\n116: | 13 | (Conditional) Collapse the host-adapter spawn and the CLI spawn | `runtime/hooks/codex/shared.ts` and Devin/Cursor siblings; `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | About 74 ms per Claude prompt (205 → ~131 ms) | Only after rank 4's cold-start measurement shows it matters; hook-latency median ≤ 135 ms, CLI fallback tests pass |\n117: | 14 | Small guards: native-spelling column in the 006 surface table; once-per-command clause unconditional; 44-row head-length matrix; session brief-cost script; command read-cost report flagging `start` docs over 8 KB; machine-readable `write_targets` | `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`; `AGENTS.md`; `ADV/tests`; new `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `measure-command-read-cost.mjs`; `*/command-metadata.json` | Each makes one silent drift visible (5 of 44 docs over 8 KB today; worst head 136 of 140 bytes) | Each script prints its row counts; a 141-byte fixture fails; `repeated 0` in the post arm |\n118: \n119: ## Eliminated Alternatives\n120: \n121: | Approach | Reason Eliminated | Evidence | Iteration(s) |\n122: |---|---|---|---|\n123: | \"Most runtimes have no hook wired\" | Five of six have a live path; Codex and Devin proxy the Claude adapter | Delivery inventory §4 | cross-cli 1 |\n124: | \"Codex declined the offered command\" | Codex received no brief: hooks unapproved, 0 of 6 transcripts with `Advisor:` | `.codex/README.md:54` | cross-cli 1-2 |\n125: | \"The hook is too slow, so the brief is dropped\" | Warm median ~200 ms against 2.5 s; only the cold path fails | `measured-2026-11-12.txt` | cross-cli 1; performance 1-3 |\n126: | \"A `COMMAND:` line proves an offer\" | DSH emitted one with the advisor off | runs-pre.jsonl | cross-cli 2 |\n127: | Trim the comment-hygiene directive to save tokens | Carries a repo hard block; suppressed after the first message; at most 54 tokens per session | `render.ts:162` | ux 1, 5; performance 4 |\n128: | Rename `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` | Blocked by decision Q025; rank 7 and 9 reach the same commands | decision-record | ux 3 |\n129: | Semantic or persisted prompt cache, new vector precompute | Pays an embedding to decide a hit; vectors already exist; no field hit rate measurable | `prompt-cache.ts:16`, `metrics.ts:319` | performance 4 |\n130: | Longer cold timeout | Trades a fast fail-open for a 5 s first-prompt stall | — | performance 3 |\n131: | Show the degraded meaning lane in the brief | Ruled out by decision Q037 | decision-record | ux 4 |\n132: | Add a recommendation leg to `/doctor:setup` | Route invariant forbids starting the daemon; the proof goes in the install guide | `doctor-setup.yaml` | ux 4 |\n133: | Re-run the before arm in research | Phase 007 owns the arm; research may not start CLI runs | steer.md | ux 2 |\n134: | Treat Claude's low rate as a brief failure | Same brief yields 3 of 4 read-only starts and 0 of 8 mutating starts | runs-pre.jsonl | ux 2 |\n135: \n136: ## Divergence Map\n137: \n138: No divergent pivots were taken in any lineage. Saturated directions: directive trimming, the `create` rename, caching and precompute, steady-state latency. Remaining frontier: the post-arm behaviour of the planned head (needs ranks 2-3 first), the cold daemon start time (needs a sandbox socket measurement), OpenCode's folder rule for `skill.md`, Devin's delivery observability, and the Codex and DSH smoke runs.\n139: \n140: ## 12. Open Questions\n141: \n142: 1. Does an offer move mutating starts on Claude and Codex? Only the post arm with ranks 2-3 in place can say.\n143: 2. What does a cold first prompt cost end to end? Unmeasured under this run's rules (no daemon or ollama control); it bounds the gain of ranks 4 and 13.\n144: 3. Does OpenCode collapse a folder that holds `skill.md`?\n145: 4. How does a failed host invocation (a model typing `/create:readme` in Codex) show up? It leaves no tool call and no scored fact today.\n146: 5. Is the Devin brief delivered? The shim is wired; the sampled records cannot show it.\n147: 6. Should the embed model stay warm (`keep_alive`) against phase 008's cold-by-design choice? Operator decision.\n148: \n149: ## 13. References\n150: \n151: - Parent packet `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/`: `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`, `goal.md`; `plan.md` and `tasks.md` of `005`-`008`; `007/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`, `007/scratch/g5/result.txt`; `008/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt`\n152: - Lineage syntheses: `lineages/ux/research.md`, `lineages/performance/research.md`, `lineages/cross-cli/research.md`; iterations under `lineages/<label>/iterations/`\n153: - Merged registry `findings-registry.json` (67 key findings), attribution `fanout-attribution.md`, resource map `resource-map.md`\n154: - Runtime surfaces: `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/README.md`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`\n155: - Advisor code: `runtime/lib/render.ts`, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`; `system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/{auto-select.ts,registry.ts,adapters/ollama.ts}`\n156: \n157: ## 14. Answered Questions\n158: \n159: - What stops a model from starting an offered command, per runtime: Codex and DSH never get the brief on a normal install; elsewhere no offer exists yet (pre-005), and capability judgment splits read-only from mutating commands. Answered.\n160: - Where hook time goes and what removes the fail-open: answered (§7, rank 4).\n161: - Token cost per prompt and per start: answered (brief 60-75 tokens; started document ~1,131 tokens median).\n162: - Discovery defects: answered (G5, three spellings, no visibility check).\n163: - External install path: answered (no Codex approval step, no DSH, existing hook configs win, setup SKIPs cold).\n164: \n165: ## 15. Limitations and Confidence\n166: \n167: - Executor is a flash model; numbers it reports were spot-checked by the orchestrator for the load-bearing items (Codex approval, DSH flag, cascade and cold-start timeouts, no `keep_alive`, `/doctor:setup` SKIP, `skill.md` presence). Others carry the lineage's citation only.\n168: - The before arm grew during the run; §3 is the single snapshot used for ranking.\n169: - Gains for ranks 4, 7 and 13 are estimates until the cold-start and Pi A/B measurements exist.\n170: - The ux lineage ran the real hook 47 times, which appended telemetry rows under `$TMPDIR/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/` (outside the repository).\n171: \n172: ## 16. Implementation Decision\n173: \n174: Recommended next packet: ranks 1-6 as one reachability-and-attribution phase after 007's after arm, because ranks 2-3 are required for that arm to be evidence and ranks 1, 4, 5 and 6 decide whether a brief exists at all on four runtimes. Ranks 7-12 follow once the post arm shows which runtimes still decline. Rank 13 waits on the cold-start measurement. Operator decision needed on `keep_alive` (§12 Q6).\n175: \n176: ## 17. Convergence Report\n177: \n178: - Stop reason: per lineage — `cross-cli` converged after 3 iterations (all 5 questions answered); `performance` reached its 5-iteration cap (last ratio 0.45); `ux` reached its 5-iteration cap (ratios 0.83-0.90).\n179: - Total iterations: 13 (ux 5, performance 5, cross-cli 3)\n180: - Questions answered: cross-cli 5/5, performance 5/5, ux 4/5 substantive (KQ1 half answered: model-side behaviour needs the post arm)\n181: - Convergence threshold: 0.05\n182: - Divergence summary: no divergent pivots recorded"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539590947,"end":1794539590962}}}}
