 - The embedder measurements of phase 008 (`../008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt`).\n100: - The runtime surfaces and advisor code that `research/research.md` section 13 lists, among them `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.codex/README.md`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, `runtime/lib/render.ts` and `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`.\n101: \n102: ### In Scope\n103: - Run a fan-out deep research over the three lanes and merge the lineages into one ranked list in `research/research.md`.\n104: - Rerun the research against the built state of phases 005 to 008 and the after arm of phase 007 until it converges.\n105: - Record a disposition for each ranked recommendation in `tasks.md`.\n106: \n107: ### Out of Scope\n108: - Any change to code, commands, hooks, install guides or `AGENTS.md`. Each recommendation that is accepted is built in a new phase with its own spec.\n109: - Reading holdout prompt rows from any corpus file. The research rules in `research/research.md` section 2 forbid it.\n110: - Starting CLI runs for the behaviour arms. Phase 007 owns the arms.\n111: \n112: ### Files to Change\n113: \n114: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n115: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n116: | `research/` | Create | Lineage state, iterations and the merged synthesis written by the deep-research run |\n117: | `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` | Create | This packet's documents and the disposition table |\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n123: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n124: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n125: \n126: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n127: \n128: | ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n129: |----|-------------|---------------------|\n130: | REQ-001 | Segment one merges all three lineages into one ranked list | `research/research.md` section 9 holds 14 numbered rows and `research/orchestration-summary.json` reports 3 succeeded and 0 failed |\n131: | REQ-002 | Each ranked recommendation is built in a new phase or declined with a reason | Every row of the disposition table in `tasks.md` reads `built in <phase>` or `declined: <reason>` |\n132: \n133: ### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n134: \n135: | ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n136: |----|-------------|---------------------|\n137: | REQ-003 | Segment two reruns the research against the built phases 005 to 008 and the phase 007 after arm until it converges | A second merged synthesis under `research/` records its stop reason as converged, and the open questions in `research/research.md` section 12 are answered or carried forward with a reason |\n138: | REQ-004 | No document in this child reads or prints a holdout prompt row | `rg -n 'holdout' spec.md plan.md tasks.md` shows only rule text, never a prompt |\n139: <!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n140: \n141: ---\n142: \n143: <!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n144: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n145: \n146: - **SC-001**: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n147: - **SC-002**: The disposition table in `tasks.md` has 14 rows and none has an empty `Disposition` cell when this child closes.\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n153: ## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n154: \n155: | Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n156: |------|------|--------|------------|\n157: | Dependency | Phases 005 to 008 built and the phase 007 after arm recorded | Segment two has no built state to read until they land | Segment two stays open in `tasks.md` and starts only when phase 007 records its after arm |\n158: | Risk | The executor is a flash model and some of its numbers carry only the lineage's citation | Med | `research/research.md` section 15 marks which claims the orchestrator re-checked. A phase that builds a recommendation measures its own baseline before it claims the gain |\n159: | Risk | The before arm grew while segment one ran | Low | Ranking uses the single snapshot in `research/research.md` section 3 |\n160: <!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n161: \n162: ---\n163: \n164: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n165: ## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n166: \n167: - The six open questions in `research/research.md` section 12 carry into segment two. Question 6, whether the embed model should stay warm against the cold-by-design choice of phase 008, is an operator decision.\n168: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539597671,"end":1794539597684}}}}
