{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794539752563,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"id":"prt_1d2e78c73001rX1qDfXFP6ciak","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2e7866d001X40WWWBe5G3LUF","type":"step-start","snapshot":"fbd8b9fa7ac953204ebe99e52fb9fc0b9874ae95"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539754990,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e790b0002s6W5iMfoFhpvii","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2e7866d001X40WWWBe5G3LUF","type":"tool","id":"call_a2c13927636e476e9f6a7b80","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '50,75p' AGENTS.md && echo \"== bytes ==\" && awk 'NR>=55 && NR<=70' AGENTS.md | wc -c && echo \"== hook doc policy table ==\" && rg -n \"Starting a surfaced command|parent-named|\\brun\\b.*\\bstart\\b.*\\bask\\b\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -20"},"output":"2. Classify intent: Research or Implementation\n3. Parse the request; judge confidence against the Confidence Thresholds below — the single scale, no second one.\n4. Below the proceed bar → INVESTIGATE (max 3 iterations) → ESCALATE per §7.\n\n#### Confidence Thresholds\n\n| Confidence | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| **≥80%** | Proceed with citable source |\n| **40-79%** | Proceed with caveats |\n| **<40%** | Ask for clarification or mark \"UNKNOWN\" |\n| **Override** | Blockers/conflicts → ask regardless of score |\n\n#### GATE 2: SKILL ROUTING [REQUIRED for non-trivial tasks]\n1. A) Primary: use the Skill Advisor Hook brief the runtime surfaced, when present. See `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n2. B) Direct call: run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n3. C) Cite user's explicit direction: \"User specified: [exact quote]\"\n- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed\n- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`\n- **Artifact trigger — binds on what you write, regardless of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs (`system-spec-kit`'s) and the gitignored runtime state Gate 3 exempts, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what its ROUTER.md resolves, per Gate 5's loading rule. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract wrong for this case is followed and amended, per PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4.\n- Output: `SKILL ROUTING: [result]` or `SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]`; when the artifact trigger fires, add `ARTIFACT: [skill] → [what its router resolved]`\n- Skip: trivial queries only (greetings, single-line questions). The artifact trigger skips only the §6 exemption class.\n\n#### GATE 3: SPEC FOLDER QUESTION [HARD] BLOCK — ASKED FIRST\n**Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n\n== bytes ==\n    1990\n== hook doc policy table ==\n39:5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)`. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n90:### Starting a surfaced command\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2. Classify intent: Research or Implementation\n3. Parse the request; judge confidence against the Confidence Thresholds below — the single scale, no second one.\n4. Below the proceed bar → INVESTIGATE (max 3 iterations) → ESCALATE per §7.\n\n#### Confidence Thresholds\n\n| Confidence | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| **≥80%** | Proceed with citable source |\n| **40-79%** | Proceed with caveats |\n| **<40%** | Ask for clarification or mark \"UNKNOWN\" |\n| **Override** | Blockers/conflicts → ask regardless of score |\n\n#### GATE 2: SKILL ROUTING [REQUIRED for non-trivial tasks]\n1. A) Primary: use the Skill Advisor Hook brief the runtime surfaced, when present. See `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n2. B) Direct call: run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n3. C) Cite user's explicit direction: \"User specified: [exact quote]\"\n- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed\n- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`\n- **Artifact trigger — binds on what you write, regardless of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs (`system-spec-kit`'s) and the gitignored runtime state Gate 3 exempts, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what its ROUTER.md resolves, per Gate 5's loading rule. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract wrong for this case is followed and amended, per PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4.\n- Output: `SKILL ROUTING: [result]` or `SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]`; when the artifact trigger fires, add `ARTIFACT: [skill] → [what its router resolved]`\n- Skip: trivial queries only (greetings, single-line questions). The artifact trigger skips only the §6 exemption class.\n\n#### GATE 3: SPEC FOLDER QUESTION [HARD] BLOCK — ASKED FIRST\n**Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n\n== bytes ==\n    1990\n== hook doc policy table ==\n39:5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)`. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n90:### Starting a surfaced command\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '50,75p' AGENTS.md && echo \\\"== bytes ==\\\" && awk 'NR>=55 && NR<=70' AGENTS.md | wc -c && echo \\\"== hook doc policy table ==\\\" && rg -n \\\"Starting a surfaced command|parent-named|\\\\brun\\\\b.*\\\\bstart\\\\b.*\\\\bask\\\\b\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539753648,"end":1794539754990}}}}
