{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539763020,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e7b2010016QAHCc4Cv1Ieln","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2e79b24001zz63njQzmKsZei","type":"tool","id":"call_4c3b7aa41133459484189fc9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && wc -l INSTALL-SKILLED.md && rg -n \"CLAUDE\\.md|AGENTS\\.md|Codex|hooks|cursor|devin|dsh|opencode|pi\\b\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -40"},"output":"     366 INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n40:Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n57:Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n65:Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n67:DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n69:Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n106:It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n108:To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n112:The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n131:2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n133:4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n136:allow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n146:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n148:| 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n165:- **Per runtime:** `.claude` with `.mcp.json`, `.opencode`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin` or `.pi`.\n216:git archive <commit> .skilled .claude .opencode | tar -x -C /path/to/your-project\n312:A re-pin copies `.skilled` and the runtime folders. It never copies a root file such as `AGENTS.md`, so your project's version survives. Each upstream change it skips prints as a `not-copied` line. Copy those over by hand if you want them. A top-level link, such as `specs`, is skipped without a line.\n364:- [overlay-guard README](.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/README.md): the hook that protects overlay-owned files.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"     366 INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n40:Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n57:Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n65:Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n67:DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n69:Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n106:It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n108:To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n112:The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n131:2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n133:4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n136:allow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n146:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n148:| 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n165:- **Per runtime:** `.claude` with `.mcp.json`, `.opencode`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin` or `.pi`.\n216:git archive <commit> .skilled .claude .opencode | tar -x -C /path/to/your-project\n312:A re-pin copies `.skilled` and the runtime folders. It never copies a root file such as `AGENTS.md`, so your project's version survives. Each upstream change it skips prints as a `not-copied` line. Copy those over by hand if you want them. A top-level link, such as `specs`, is skipped without a line.\n364:- [overlay-guard README](.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/README.md): the hook that protects overlay-owned files.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && wc -l INSTALL-SKILLED.md && rg -n \\\"CLAUDE\\\\.md|AGENTS\\\\.md|Codex|hooks|cursor|devin|dsh|opencode|pi\\\\b\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539762177,"end":1794539763020}}}}
