{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539870284,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e90bf3002DuCFfTb7zu5swR","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2e8ff150013lWv3sWBXHyt7I","type":"tool","id":"call_8c79b0a3c83241f1a77cff89","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-2 (UX and cost lane, segment two)\ndescription: Tracks the ux-cost-2 lineage of the segment-two command-surfacing research: focus, questions, known context and boundaries.\ntrigger_phrases: []\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n# Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-2\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nLane label `ux-cost-2`: what the person and the model read, and what it costs. Segment two of the command-surfacing research, run against the built state of phases 005, 006, 008 and 010 and the in-flight phase 011.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nUX and cost lane. Which changes to the brief wording, the run/start/ask wording, the install and setup path for an external repository, and the embedder keep-alive raise how often a plain request is started on its expected command, and at what byte, token, memory and latency cost? Anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 and 011 already built or plan is excluded.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] KQ1: Which words in the delivered brief and its policy definition reach the model, and which reach only AGENTS.md?\n- [ ] KQ2: What does the brief cost per prompt after phase 005, and which repeated bytes can move to once per session?\n- [ ] KQ3: What must an external repository install do so a plain request gets an offered command with a usable policy?\n- [ ] KQ4: Should the semantic embedder be kept warm, and at what memory and latency cost against the 750 ms deadline?\n- [ ] KQ5: Which ranked changes raise started-when-useful per unit of risk without lowering any floor?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 or 011 built or plan: the command contract and brief head, the Gate 2 bullet, the Codex approval step, DSH reachability, the hook-wiring check, offer recording, the attributable scorer, the argued-route lookup, typed delivery 44 of 44, the visibility guard, hook health in status, the setup leg and the brief-cost script.\n- Changing scorer weights, the `/speckit:resume` disambiguation, the Python scorer or any corpus label.\n- Starting a model CLI session, an arena, a daemon or ollama; running the full test suite.\n- Reading or printing the prompt text of any row whose split is holdout. Tune and none rows may be read.\n- Editing any file outside this lineage directory.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Three iterations complete with all five key questions answered or explicitly carried forward.\n- A fourth iteration only if the third leaves a load-bearing claim unresolved or a ranking conflict open.\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nStart with KQ1 and KQ2: render the brief head byte-for-byte from `runtime/lib/render.ts` and `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, separate the constant directive from the per-command head, and establish which definition of `run`, `start` and `ask` a runtime actually receives.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Measured facts carried from the dispatch and the built phases\n\n- Start rate, before to after: claude 3/12 to 4/12, codex 0/12 to 0/12, pi 0/11 to 2/10, devin 1/8 to 3/9, opencode 2/7 to 1/5, dsh 6/12 to 6/12. Unsafe runs 9 to 4. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:132]\n- The expected command was offered on 3 of 16 plain tune rows and `/doctor:helper` on 2 more; nothing on 11. When offered, the model usually took it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-post-final.jsonl]\n- Plain recall on the tune split is 9 of 45 on phrases and 14 of 45 with the real embedder. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:131]\n- `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01` gets no command because the system-deep-loop hub defers on the mode; three runtimes then improvise a multi-pass audit and write. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:133]\n- Brief delivery after: claude 24/24, devin 24/24, pi 24/24, dsh 23/23, opencode plugin loaded 24 times with no stored trace, codex 0/24 because a fresh checkout's project hooks are unapproved. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:135]\n- The shared session readers under `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/` drop injected context, so `briefDelivered` reads unknown for devin, dsh and opencode. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:170]\n- Claude Code reads only the global instruction file, so a project without a CLAUDE.md never sees AGENTS.md Gate 2. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130]\n- The `COMMAND:` line the Gate 2 bullet asks for appears in 0 to 3 of 24 runs per runtime. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-post-final.jsonl]\n- Embedder cost: 262 MB on disk, about 304 MB loaded, warm 4.8 ms, cold first call 538.53 ms, prompt embedding deadline 750 ms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt]\n- The delivery prefix to the last AGENTS.md anchor is 16092 of 16384 bytes, which leaves 292 bytes. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/implementation-summary.md:166]\n- The brief is 242-298 bytes and 60-75 tokens, of which 233 bytes is the constant directive. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:82]\n\n### Built-state pointers\n\n- `runtime/lib/render.ts` renders the head and the directive block; `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`; `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 holds the 463-byte command bullet.\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` is the external-repository path; `/doctor:agents-md embed` folds and removes a project `CLAUDE.md`; the agents-md check expects a project CLAUDE.md to be absent, a symlink or a pointer.\n- The prompt embed path is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: `render.ts` (`commandLabel`, `capWithCompanion`, `HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE`), `command-attach.ts` (`COMMAND_ROWS`), `AGENTS.md` (Gate 2 bullet), `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (Steps 1-2), `agents-md-embed.cjs` (ALLOWLIST, FOLDED_COPIES), `agents-md-check.cjs` (runtime copies), `semantic-shadow.ts`, `shared/embeddings/registry.ts`, `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`.\n- Constraints: no scorer weight changes; no write outside the lineage; no model CLI session, arena, daemon or ollama control; holdout prompt text never read.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 4\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: this lineage's own `research.md`; the parent merge owns the combined synthesis\n- Lifecycle branches: `new` only for this lineage\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: not used in a detached lineage\n- Started: 2026-11-13T05:05:00Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-2 (UX and cost lane, segment two)\\ndescription: Tracks the ux-cost-2 lineage of the segment-two command-surfacing research: focus, questions, known context and boundaries.\\ntrigger_phrases: []\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n# Deep Research Strategy - ux-cost-2\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\nLane label `ux-cost-2`: what the person and the model read, and what it costs. Segment two of the command-surfacing research, run against the built state of phases 005, 006, 008 and 010 and the in-flight phase 011.\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nUX and cost lane. Which changes to the brief wording, the run/start/ask wording, the install and setup path for an external repository, and the embedder keep-alive raise how often a plain request is started on its expected command, and at what byte, token, memory and latency cost? Anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 and 011 already built or plan is excluded.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] KQ1: Which words in the delivered brief and its policy definition reach the model, and which reach only AGENTS.md?\\n- [ ] KQ2: What does the brief cost per prompt after phase 005, and which repeated bytes can move to once per session?\\n- [ ] KQ3: What must an external repository install do so a plain request gets an offered command with a usable policy?\\n- [ ] KQ4: Should the semantic embedder be kept warm, and at what memory and latency cost against the 750 ms deadline?\\n- [ ] KQ5: Which ranked changes raise started-when-useful per unit of risk without lowering any floor?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 or 011 built or plan: the command contract and brief head, the Gate 2 bullet, the Codex approval step, DSH reachability, the hook-wiring check, offer recording, the attributable scorer, the argued-route lookup, typed delivery 44 of 44, the visibility guard, hook health in status, the setup leg and the brief-cost script.\\n- Changing scorer weights, the `/speckit:resume` disambiguation, the Python scorer or any corpus label.\\n- Starting a model CLI session, an arena, a daemon or ollama; running the full test suite.\\n- Reading or printing the prompt text of any row whose split is holdout. Tune and none rows may be read.\\n- Editing any file outside this lineage directory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Three iterations complete with all five key questions answered or explicitly carried forward.\\n- A fourth iteration only if the third leaves a load-bearing claim unresolved or a ranking conflict open.\\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nStart with KQ1 and KQ2: render the brief head byte-for-byte from `runtime/lib/render.ts` and `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, separate the constant directive from the per-command head, and establish which definition of `run`, `start` and `ask` a runtime actually receives.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Measured facts carried from the dispatch and the built phases\\n\\n- Start rate, before to after: claude 3/12 to 4/12, codex 0/12 to 0/12, pi 0/11 to 2/10, devin 1/8 to 3/9, opencode 2/7 to 1/5, dsh 6/12 to 6/12. Unsafe runs 9 to 4. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:132]\\n- The expected command was offered on 3 of 16 plain tune rows and `/doctor:helper` on 2 more; nothing on 11. When offered, the model usually took it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-post-final.jsonl]\\n- Plain recall on the tune split is 9 of 45 on phrases and 14 of 45 with the real embedder. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:131]\\n- `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01` gets no command because the system-deep-loop hub defers on the mode; three runtimes then improvise a multi-pass audit and write. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:133]\\n- Brief delivery after: claude 24/24, devin 24/24, pi 24/24, dsh 23/23, opencode plugin loaded 24 times with no stored trace, codex 0/24 because a fresh checkout's project hooks are unapproved. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:135]\\n- The shared session readers under `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/` drop injected context, so `briefDelivered` reads unknown for devin, dsh and opencode. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:170]\\n- Claude Code reads only the global instruction file, so a project without a CLAUDE.md never sees AGENTS.md Gate 2. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130]\\n- The `COMMAND:` line the Gate 2 bullet asks for appears in 0 to 3 of 24 runs per runtime. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-post-final.jsonl]\\n- Embedder cost: 262 MB on disk, about 304 MB loaded, warm 4.8 ms, cold first call 538.53 ms, prompt embedding deadline 750 ms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt]\\n- The delivery prefix to the last AGENTS.md anchor is 16092 of 16384 bytes, which leaves 292 bytes. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/implementation-summary.md:166]\\n- The brief is 242-298 bytes and 60-75 tokens, of which 233 bytes is the constant directive. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:82]\\n\\n### Built-state pointers\\n\\n- `runtime/lib/render.ts` renders the head and the directive block; `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`; `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 holds the 463-byte command bullet.\\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` is the external-repository path; `/doctor:agents-md embed` folds and removes a project `CLAUDE.md`; the agents-md check expects a project CLAUDE.md to be absent, a symlink or a pointer.\\n- The prompt embed path is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: `render.ts` (`commandLabel`, `capWithCompanion`, `HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE`), `command-attach.ts` (`COMMAND_ROWS`), `AGENTS.md` (Gate 2 bullet), `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (Steps 1-2), `agents-md-embed.cjs` (ALLOWLIST, FOLDED_COPIES), `agents-md-check.cjs` (runtime copies), `semantic-shadow.ts`, `shared/embeddings/registry.ts`, `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`.\\n- Constraints: no scorer weight changes; no write outside the lineage; no model CLI session, arena, daemon or ollama control; holdout prompt text never read.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 4\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research.md ownership: this lineage's own `research.md`; the parent merge owns the combined synthesis\\n- Lifecycle branches: `new` only for this lineage\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: not used in a detached lineage\\n- Started: 2026-11-13T05:05:00Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539850739,"end":1794539870284}}}}
