{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540106624,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ecf038001MY8pyvnBAn7nvZ","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2ec7e54001fvtiGSxs5nU1w2","type":"tool","id":"call_fb57c35f7b6b41538aa8f63e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '20,45p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml && echo \"== presentation ==\" && rg -n -i \"claude|remove|pointer|copy\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt | head -12"},"output":"  never_commit: true\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  read_only: false\n  allowed_targets:\n    - \"AGENTS.md, the root document: created when the repository has none, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block, and left alone when it already matches\"\n    - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and removed by default; kept, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given\"\n    - \".codex/AGENTS.md, folded into the block and removed\"\n    - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n    - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n    - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n    - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n    - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n    - \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs and its lib/, which own the composition and never change here\"\n    - \"a rule file a REPO RULES.md row points at, which is authored through the create-repo-rule route and never by this one\"\n    - \"the git index, history and remotes\"\n  invariant: \"Nothing is written until the plan has printed its digest and the operator has answered yes to that plan. The plan call composes in memory and writes nothing, the apply refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, and every path the run touches is copied to the backup before the first byte. The proof that no repository line was dropped runs against the bytes now on disk, and a violation restores from the backup automatically. A no at the question ends the run with STATUS=CANCELLED and nothing written.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n== presentation ==\n12:| A flag none of the three targets accepts | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `check accepts --json and --root <dir>; embed accepts --dry-run, --root <dir>, --plan-digest <digest>, --keep-claude-md, --remove-claude-md and --create-router; restore accepts --run <dir>, --yes and --dry-run.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n64:A1  [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  install state: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n118:The plan section quotes the engine's own lines: its `[agents-md-embed] plan for <root> (state: <state>)` line, one `target <path>: <create|replace|remove|unchanged|absent>` line per path, its `note:` lines, a `diff` per path it would write, the new block between its `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the `budget:` line, each `finding:` line, the `preservation:` line, the `backup:` folder, its `backup-fallback:` line when one prints, the `undo:` command and the `plan-digest:` line. `absent` means the path is not there, so nothing is written to it and the note beside it says why it stays absent.\n123:State: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n152:The restore plan is the engine's own dry run of one run's record, so it names what will be put back, what will be removed, and each folder that removal leaves empty.\n159:Remove: [one line per path the recorded run created, or none]\n161:Folders: [one line per folder the recorded run created and an empty restore removes, or none]\n168:A folder the recorded run had to create for a new file gets its own folder line, and the restore removes it only once it is empty again. The line names the folder, never its contents.\n182:Files changed: [each path the apply printed as wrote or removed]\n183:Pointer sync: [the engine's pointer-sync line]\n188:Undo: [the engine's undo block, quoted whole: its Undo: line, its restore command and one copy line per overwritten file]\n189:Next: [the repair the lines above name, or none: a nonzero pointer-sync ends here with /doctor:runtime-mirrors]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  never_commit: true\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  read_only: false\n  allowed_targets:\n    - \"AGENTS.md, the root document: created when the repository has none, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block, and left alone when it already matches\"\n    - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and removed by default; kept, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given\"\n    - \".codex/AGENTS.md, folded into the block and removed\"\n    - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n    - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n    - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n    - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n    - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n    - \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs and its lib/, which own the composition and never change here\"\n    - \"a rule file a REPO RULES.md row points at, which is authored through the create-repo-rule route and never by this one\"\n    - \"the git index, history and remotes\"\n  invariant: \"Nothing is written until the plan has printed its digest and the operator has answered yes to that plan. The plan call composes in memory and writes nothing, the apply refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, and every path the run touches is copied to the backup before the first byte. The proof that no repository line was dropped runs against the bytes now on disk, and a violation restores from the backup automatically. A no at the question ends the run with STATUS=CANCELLED and nothing written.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n== presentation ==\n12:| A flag none of the three targets accepts | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `check accepts --json and --root <dir>; embed accepts --dry-run, --root <dir>, --plan-digest <digest>, --keep-claude-md, --remove-claude-md and --create-router; restore accepts --run <dir>, --yes and --dry-run.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n64:A1  [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  install state: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n118:The plan section quotes the engine's own lines: its `[agents-md-embed] plan for <root> (state: <state>)` line, one `target <path>: <create|replace|remove|unchanged|absent>` line per path, its `note:` lines, a `diff` per path it would write, the new block between its `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the `budget:` line, each `finding:` line, the `preservation:` line, the `backup:` folder, its `backup-fallback:` line when one prints, the `undo:` command and the `plan-digest:` line. `absent` means the path is not there, so nothing is written to it and the note beside it says why it stays absent.\n123:State: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n152:The restore plan is the engine's own dry run of one run's record, so it names what will be put back, what will be removed, and each folder that removal leaves empty.\n159:Remove: [one line per path the recorded run created, or none]\n161:Folders: [one line per folder the recorded run created and an empty restore removes, or none]\n168:A folder the recorded run had to create for a new file gets its own folder line, and the restore removes it only once it is empty again. The line names the folder, never its contents.\n182:Files changed: [each path the apply printed as wrote or removed]\n183:Pointer sync: [the engine's pointer-sync line]\n188:Undo: [the engine's undo block, quoted whole: its Undo: line, its restore command and one copy line per overwritten file]\n189:Next: [the repair the lines above name, or none: a nonzero pointer-sync ends here with /doctor:runtime-mirrors]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '20,45p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml && echo \\\"== presentation ==\\\" && rg -n -i \\\"claude|remove|pointer|copy\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540105784,"end":1794540106624}}}}
