{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540124945,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ed35ff001HI6vSmP5Mo1AZB","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2ecf865001YWKguSvfPjA051","type":"tool","id":"call_e5e2299efbae4739b25cdbac","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md && rg -n \"\\\"path\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md\\\"\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json && rg -n \"Claude reads the root document directly\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json && rg -n \"HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE = |DIRECTIVES_LABEL = |const head = \\`Advisor\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts"},"output":"68:- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`\n738:      \"path\": \"CLAUDE.md\",\n744:      \"why\": \"Claude reads the root document directly, and Cursor and Hermes load both files, so a full copy either double-loads or drifts.\"\n127:export const HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE = '\\n- Comment hygiene [HARD BLOCK]: NEVER embed ADR-/REQ-/CHK-/task-ids or spec paths in code comments — forbidden regardless of instruction. Write the durable WHY instead. Pre-commit gate blocks violations.';\n133:export const DIRECTIVES_LABEL = '\\nDirectives:';\n575:      const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; ambiguous: ${topLabel} `\n588:  const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; use ${topLabel} `\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"68:- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`\n738:      \"path\": \"CLAUDE.md\",\n744:      \"why\": \"Claude reads the root document directly, and Cursor and Hermes load both files, so a full copy either double-loads or drifts.\"\n127:export const HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE = '\\n- Comment hygiene [HARD BLOCK]: NEVER embed ADR-/REQ-/CHK-/task-ids or spec paths in code comments — forbidden regardless of instruction. Write the durable WHY instead. Pre-commit gate blocks violations.';\n133:export const DIRECTIVES_LABEL = '\\nDirectives:';\n575:      const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; ambiguous: ${topLabel} `\n588:  const head = `Advisor: ${result.freshness}; use ${topLabel} `\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"Command in the brief\\\" AGENTS.md && rg -n \\\"\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CLAUDE.md\\\\\\\"\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json && rg -n \\\"Claude reads the root document directly\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json && rg -n \\\"HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE = |DIRECTIVES_LABEL = |const head = \\\\`Advisor\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540123647,"end":1794540124945}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794540126492,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"id":"prt_1d2ed411c001oBXEYGHSjsZK03","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2ecf865001YWKguSvfPjA051","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"abb7547455456e675cc6b78c9ca33d8fce0e4453","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":3846,"output":174,"reasoning":1457,"cache":{"read":196608,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794540133523,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"id":"prt_1d2ed5c93001MRhZWOnpEikUws","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2ed412a001mVWiOvVYjzX6JY","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d5ffc00975f5d53931a936e1815357b09daaace3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540150379,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ed5c96002QQOpnDsHVyIa67","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2ed412a001mVWiOvVYjzX6JY","type":"tool","id":"call_01c171e413854949b87d3a68","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 1: What the brief says, what defines it, and what it costs\n\n## Focus\n\nKQ1 and KQ2: which words in the delivered brief reach the model and which reach only `AGENTS.md`, and what the brief costs per prompt after phase 005. The iteration renders the head byte-for-byte from `runtime/lib/render.ts` and the generated `COMMAND_ROWS`, measures the constant block against the per-command head, and checks whether the brief's policy word has a definition on each delivery path. Chosen over KQ3 because every later install and wording recommendation needs the delivered-bytes baseline first.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `render.ts` end to end and computed the exact head and directive strings it returns.\n2. Parsed the generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block in `command-attach.ts` and computed head, total and character length for every row.\n3. Read the Gate 2 bullet in `AGENTS.md` and checked where the `run`/`start`/`ask` definitions live.\n4. Checked the instruction-file state of this worktree and of the Claude user config (`CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`).\n5. Read the agents-md manifest's Claude copy rule and the shadow route-only measurement path in `render.ts` / `policy-plan.ts`.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The delivered brief is 285-327 bytes per prompt, median 298: a per-command head of 67-109 bytes (median 80) plus a 218-byte constant block (`Directives:` + the comment-hygiene hard block). The constant is 73% of the median brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:127] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:133] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:60]\n\n2. The constant block is emitted on every brief, not once per session. `renderAdvisorBrief` appends `DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE` unconditionally on both the normal and the ambiguous return path, and `renderRouteOnlyAdvisorBrief` is called only from the shadow observer to compute `savedBytes`; nothing strips the block from the emitted bytes. The shadow plan therefore measures a 43-byte route-only brief that is never produced. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:588] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:406] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:314]\n\n3. Contradictory evidence on the directive's repeat cost: segment one's eliminated-alternatives table says the directive is \"suppressed after the first message; at most 54 tokens per session\", while the renderer appends it to every brief. The renderer is the emitted-byte source of truth, so the segment-one line describes the shadow measurement, not delivery. Recorded, not resolved in segment one's favour. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:127] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:594]\n\n4. The head carries the policy word but never its definition. The only definition of `run`, `start` and `ask` is the 463-byte Gate 2 bullet, and `render.ts` emits none of it. A runtime that receives the brief without `AGENTS.md` therefore receives a policy word it cannot resolve. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:234]\n\n5. On Claude Code in this worktree the definition does not arrive at all: there is no project `CLAUDE.md`, and `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is a symlink to the main checkout's `AGENTS.md` at `/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/AGENTS.md`. The after-arm Claude rows carried the brief and not the bullet, which is why their `(start)`/`(ask)` words were undefined. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130]\n\n6. Contradiction inside the install design: the agents-md manifest says \"Claude reads the root document directly\", while the measured after arm shows a project with `AGENTS.md` and no `CLAUDE.md` produced Claude rows without the bullet. Both claims are recorded; the recommendation in iteration 2 has to work under either one, which a one-line pointer does. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:744] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130]\n\n7. Head room is real but small: the longest head is 107 characters against the renderer's 320-character single-head cap, and a 40-byte addition costs 13% of the median brief while a 110-byte clause costs 37%. The policy mix is 20 `start`, 7 `run` and 17 `ask` of 44 tracked commands, so any policy gloss applies to the majority of offers. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:104] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:124]\n\n8. The two numbers in the head (`0.85/0.20 pass.`) cost about 14 bytes on every prompt and have no reader inside the brief; they are the scorer's confidence and uncertainty, and the ambiguous head repeats them for the second candidate. Removing them is a byte saving with no measurable behaviour path. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:588] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:575]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Trimming the comment-hygiene directive to save tokens: it is a repository hard block and the only place the rule reaches a brief-only session. The new measurement changes its size, not its status. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:127]\n- Emitting the route-only brief after first delivery: the shadow plan would drop the hard block exactly in the sessions where `AGENTS.md` is absent, which is the measured Claude case. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:406]\n- Replacing the confidence/uncertainty pair with prose: no measurable path, and the ambiguous head uses both numbers to compare two candidates. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:575]\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching for a per-session suppression in the emitted path: the only suppression logic (`SUPPRESSED_SAME`, `routeOnlyEligible`) feeds the shadow log, not the returned string. No emitter-side gate exists to reuse. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/policy-plan.ts:453]\n- Treating the `Brief` byte totals in segment one as per-command: they are first-render totals; the head varies by 42 bytes across commands. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:82]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"what the model reads\" has two readings, the brief bytes and the instruction file. Both were measured; the instruction file is the load-bearing one for the policy words.\n- Contradictory evidence: the segment-one suppression claim and the renderer's unconditional append (finding 3); the manifest's Claude claim and the after-arm measurement (finding 6). Neither is resolved by preference; both are carried into iteration 2.\n- Missing dependencies: none. The brief is computed from source, not from a live hook, so no daemon or model was started.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/policy-plan.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`\n- `AGENTS.md`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`\n- `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (symlink target read only)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.62\n- Questions addressed: KQ1, KQ2\n- Questions answered: KQ1, KQ2\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: computing the brief from the renderer and the generated table, rather than trusting the reported 242-298 bytes, exposed that the head is only 27% of the brief and that the constant block never shrinks. Parsing the table also made the \"room for a gloss\" question numeric instead of rhetorical.\n- What did not work and why: looking for an emitter-side suppression failed because the state machine is a measurement surface; segment one read its own shadow metric as delivery.\n- What I would do differently: read the returned string before the shadow log next time; the emitted bytes are the only cost that reaches the model.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nKQ3: the external-repository install path. The embed branch removes the project `CLAUDE.md` that the Claude Code path needs, and the install's final `/doctor:setup` does not report whether any brief was delivered, so a fresh install can finish green with a runtime at zero.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 1: What the brief says, what defines it, and what it costs\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nKQ1 and KQ2: which words in the delivered brief reach the model and which reach only `AGENTS.md`, and what the brief costs per prompt after phase 005. The iteration renders the head byte-for-byte from `runtime/lib/render.ts` and the generated `COMMAND_ROWS`, measures the constant block against the per-command head, and checks whether the brief's policy word has a definition on each delivery path. Chosen over KQ3 because every later install and wording recommendation needs the delivered-bytes baseline first.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read `render.ts` end to end and computed the exact head and directive strings it returns.\\n2. Parsed the generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block in `command-attach.ts` and computed head, total and character length for every row.\\n3. Read the Gate 2 bullet in `AGENTS.md` and checked where the `run`/`start`/`ask` definitions live.\\n4. Checked the instruction-file state of this worktree and of the Claude user config (`CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`).\\n5. Read the agents-md manifest's Claude copy rule and the shadow route-only measurement path in `render.ts` / `policy-plan.ts`.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The delivered brief is 285-327 bytes per prompt, median 298: a per-command head of 67-109 bytes (median 80) plus a 218-byte constant block (`Directives:` + the comment-hygiene hard block). The constant is 73% of the median brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:127] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:133] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:60]\\n\\n2. The constant block is emitted on every brief, not once per session. `renderAdvisorBrief` appends `DIRECTIVES_LABEL + HYGIENE_DIRECTIVE` unconditionally on both the normal and the ambiguous return path, and `renderRouteOnlyAdvisorBrief` is called only from the shadow observer to compute `savedBytes`; nothing strips the block from the emitted bytes. The shadow plan therefore measures a 43-byte route-only brief that is never produced. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:588] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:406] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:314]\\n\\n3. Contradictory evidence on the directive's repeat cost: segment one's eliminated-alternatives table says the directive is \\\"suppressed after the first message; at most 54 tokens per session\\\", while the renderer appends it to every brief. The renderer is the emitted-byte source of truth, so the segment-one line describes the shadow measurement, not delivery. Recorded, not resolved in segment one's favour. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:127] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:594]\\n\\n4. The head carries the policy word but never its definition. The only definition of `run`, `start` and `ask` is the 463-byte Gate 2 bullet, and `render.ts` emits none of it. A runtime that receives the brief without `AGENTS.md` therefore receives a policy word it cannot resolve. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:234]\\n\\n5. On Claude Code in this worktree the definition does not arrive at all: there is no project `CLAUDE.md`, and `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` is a symlink to the main checkout's `AGENTS.md` at `/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/AGENTS.md`. The after-arm Claude rows carried the brief and not the bullet, which is why their `(start)`/`(ask)` words were undefined. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130]\\n\\n6. Contradiction inside the install design: the agents-md manifest says \\\"Claude reads the root document directly\\\", while the measured after arm shows a project with `AGENTS.md` and no `CLAUDE.md` produced Claude rows without the bullet. Both claims are recorded; the recommendation in iteration 2 has to work under either one, which a one-line pointer does. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:744] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130]\\n\\n7. Head room is real but small: the longest head is 107 characters against the renderer's 320-character single-head cap, and a 40-byte addition costs 13% of the median brief while a 110-byte clause costs 37%. The policy mix is 20 `start`, 7 `run` and 17 `ask` of 44 tracked commands, so any policy gloss applies to the majority of offers. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:104] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:124]\\n\\n8. The two numbers in the head (`0.85/0.20 pass.`) cost about 14 bytes on every prompt and have no reader inside the brief; they are the scorer's confidence and uncertainty, and the ambiguous head repeats them for the second candidate. Removing them is a byte saving with no measurable behaviour path. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:588] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:575]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Trimming the comment-hygiene directive to save tokens: it is a repository hard block and the only place the rule reaches a brief-only session. The new measurement changes its size, not its status. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:127]\\n- Emitting the route-only brief after first delivery: the shadow plan would drop the hard block exactly in the sessions where `AGENTS.md` is absent, which is the measured Claude case. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:406]\\n- Replacing the confidence/uncertainty pair with prose: no measurable path, and the ambiguous head uses both numbers to compare two candidates. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:575]\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Searching for a per-session suppression in the emitted path: the only suppression logic (`SUPPRESSED_SAME`, `routeOnlyEligible`) feeds the shadow log, not the returned string. No emitter-side gate exists to reuse. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/policy-plan.ts:453]\\n- Treating the `Brief` byte totals in segment one as per-command: they are first-render totals; the head varies by 42 bytes across commands. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md:82]\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"what the model reads\\\" has two readings, the brief bytes and the instruction file. Both were measured; the instruction file is the load-bearing one for the policy words.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the segment-one suppression claim and the renderer's unconditional append (finding 3); the manifest's Claude claim and the after-arm measurement (finding 6). Neither is resolved by preference; both are carried into iteration 2.\\n- Missing dependencies: none. The brief is computed from source, not from a live hook, so no daemon or model was started.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/policy-plan.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`\\n- `AGENTS.md`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`\\n- `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (symlink target read only)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.62\\n- Questions addressed: KQ1, KQ2\\n- Questions answered: KQ1, KQ2\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: computing the brief from the renderer and the generated table, rather than trusting the reported 242-298 bytes, exposed that the head is only 27% of the brief and that the constant block never shrinks. Parsing the table also made the \\\"room for a gloss\\\" question numeric instead of rhetorical.\\n- What did not work and why: looking for an emitter-side suppression failed because the state machine is a measurement surface; segment one read its own shadow metric as delivery.\\n- What I would do differently: read the returned string before the shadow log next time; the emitted bytes are the only cost that reaches the model.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nKQ3: the external-repository install path. The embed branch removes the project `CLAUDE.md` that the Claude Code path needs, and the install's final `/doctor:setup` does not report whether any brief was delivered, so a fresh install can finish green with a runtime at zero.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540133526,"end":1794540150379}}}}
