{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540221743,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2eeafeb001NDXCr3iV5KCM0L","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2ee9eab0013PxlPk53uguYU6","type":"tool","id":"call_729fa076a3494f34b3e2da03","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"codex-hook-approval|hook-wiring-check\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/*.yaml | head -10 && echo \"== install step count ==\" && rg -n \"codex-hooks-approved|codex-hooks-unapproved\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs | head -6 && echo \"== setup presentation rows ==\" && rg -n \"advisor|runtime-mirrors\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt | head -10"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:41:  codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n== install step count ==\n186:      code: 'codex-hooks-approved',\n191:    }, ['PASS codex-hooks-approved']);\n198:    code: 'codex-hooks-unapproved',\n204:  }, [`WARN codex-hooks-unapproved ${root}`, repair]);\n== setup presentation rows ==\n33:| `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34:| `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35:| `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36:| `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37:| `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38:| `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39:| `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40:| `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n60:| runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61:| advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:41:  codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n== install step count ==\n186:      code: 'codex-hooks-approved',\n191:    }, ['PASS codex-hooks-approved']);\n198:    code: 'codex-hooks-unapproved',\n204:  }, [`WARN codex-hooks-unapproved ${root}`, repair]);\n== setup presentation rows ==\n33:| `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34:| `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35:| `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36:| `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37:| `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38:| `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39:| `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40:| `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n60:| runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61:| advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"codex-hook-approval|hook-wiring-check\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/*.yaml | head -10 && echo \\\"== install step count ==\\\" && rg -n \\\"codex-hooks-approved|codex-hooks-unapproved\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs | head -6 && echo \\\"== setup presentation rows ==\\\" && rg -n \\\"advisor|runtime-mirrors\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540220395,"end":1794540221743}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794540222816,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"id":"prt_1d2eeb960001m3e0i8jM3slWSj","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2ee9eab0013PxlPk53uguYU6","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fc94da9fd06a3dcb3fee436fb653ac79fa738b57","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1483,"output":184,"reasoning":249,"cache":{"read":211840,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794540224648,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"id":"prt_1d2eec088001jtNDQ2NCXMwhIc","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2eeb967001d7BskcczI7ueqx","type":"step-start","snapshot":"fc94da9fd06a3dcb3fee436fb653ac79fa738b57"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540250731,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2eedf5c001lhtTVQd14jDaHv","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2eeb967001d7BskcczI7ueqx","type":"tool","id":"call_d7fe090a383b41aaa75ded93","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 2: The external-repository install, and two runtimes that finish green without the brief or its policy\n\n## Focus\n\nKQ3: what an external repository install must do so a plain request gets an offered command with a usable policy. The iteration follows the two instruction-file choices in `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, the Claude copy rule in the agents-md engine and check, and the six legs of the install's final `/doctor:setup` against the measured per-runtime brief delivery.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the install guide's Step 1 and Step 2 (the embed and link choices) and the agents-md embed route's mutation boundary.\n2. Read the agents-md engine's copy handling and the check's A1 install-state and A10 runtime-copy rows.\n3. Read the symlink manifest's `CLAUDE.md` row and the two read-only hook checks.\n4. Read `/doctor:setup`'s six legs and the doctor route table, and compared them with where `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` are actually called.\n5. Re-read the after-arm delivery numbers for Claude and Codex against those install shapes.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The install offers two instruction-file shapes with opposite outcomes for Claude Code: `link` makes `CLAUDE.md` a symlink to the checkout's `AGENTS.md`, while `embed` folds a project `CLAUDE.md` into `AGENTS.md` and removes it, leaving no file named `CLAUDE.md` in the project. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json:23] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:29]\n\n2. The agents-md check is asymmetric. It has a named `claude-only` install state for a repository with `CLAUDE.md` and no `AGENTS.md`, but no state or row for the reverse shape that `embed` produces. A10 accepts `absent` as an expected `CLAUDE.md`, so an embed install with no Claude instruction file passes the check. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:217] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:738]\n\n3. The install's final step is not truthful about brief delivery. `/doctor:setup` runs six read-only legs, and none of them reports whether a runtime received a brief or whether its prompt hook is approved; the Codex approval check runs only under `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, and the hook-wiring check only under `/doctor:symlink check`. A fresh Codex install can therefore print `STATUS=OK` with 0 of 24 briefs delivered. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:54] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:41] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60]\n\n4. The measured after arm lands exactly on those two shapes: Codex delivered 0 of 24 briefs because a fresh checkout's project hooks are unapproved, and Claude delivered 24 of 24 briefs but 0 of 24 Gate 2 bullets because the arena had no project `CLAUDE.md` and the global file points at the main checkout. Two of six runtimes reach a nominally successful install with either no brief or no policy definition. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:135]\n\n5. The cheap repair fits both readings of Claude's instruction loading: a one-line `@AGENTS.md` pointer is not a copy, so it cannot double-load or drift, and the manifest's own expected set already lists `pointer` for `CLAUDE.md`. No validator change is needed; only the engine's default and the check's missing row. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:738]\n\n6. The install guide does not tell the person what the instruction-file choice costs per runtime. Step 1 says `embed` \"adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`\" and step 2 repeats it; neither says `embed` removes `CLAUDE.md`, and neither names Claude as the runtime that depends on it. [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:133] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:146]\n\n7. Both repairs are display and file-authoring changes with no process and no scorer path: one 12-byte pointer written at embed time, one check row that reads the project `CLAUDE.md`, and one `/doctor:setup` line that calls the two existing read-only checks. [INFERENCE: based on the embed engine's allowlist and the setup legs' read-only invariant]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Write the operator's global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` from the install path: outside the repository, declared report-only by the manifest, and it changes what every session on the machine loads. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:777]\n- Keep a full `CLAUDE.md` copy from `embed`: the manifest's own reason says a full copy double-loads or drifts; a pointer avoids both. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:744]\n- Leave the Codex signal to `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`: a person who ran the six printed install steps has no reason to run a seventh command, so the zero stays silent. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:54]\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a setup leg that already covers brief delivery: the advisor leg checks `advisor_status` freshness, not a delivered brief, and the embedder leg checks the semantic lane. Neither reads a run log or a hook approval. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:57]\n- Looking for a check that fails on the embed shape: A1 only names `claude-only`, and A10 accepts `absent`, so both rows pass. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:217]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"external repository setup\" could mean the link engine, the instruction file or the hook approval. All three are on the printed install path, so all three were measured; the instruction file is the one with a runtime-specific zero.\n- Contradictory evidence: carried from iteration 1 between the manifest's \"Claude reads the root document directly\" and the measured arena. The pointer recommendation is deliberately valid under both.\n- Missing dependencies: none; all reads were local and no command wrote outside the lineage.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.72\n- Questions addressed: KQ3\n- Questions answered: KQ3\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: following the printed install steps in order, then asking what each final check actually reads, found a green status that no measured runtime supports. Comparing the two instruction-file shapes explained why the same brief behaved differently on Claude between the main checkout and the arena.\n- What did not work and why: searching for an existing brief-delivery leg failed because every leg is a component check; none composes \"the runtime can receive a brief\" from the hook file plus the approval plus the instruction file.\n- What I would do differently: start from the final status line and walk backwards; the misleading green is the finding, and the file shapes are its cause.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nKQ4 and KQ5: the embedder keep-alive decision with its memory and latency numbers, then the ranking. The install-side findings already supply two of the ranked items; the ranking needs the cost side measured before it can order them.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 2: The external-repository install, and two runtimes that finish green without the brief or its policy\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nKQ3: what an external repository install must do so a plain request gets an offered command with a usable policy. The iteration follows the two instruction-file choices in `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, the Claude copy rule in the agents-md engine and check, and the six legs of the install's final `/doctor:setup` against the measured per-runtime brief delivery.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the install guide's Step 1 and Step 2 (the embed and link choices) and the agents-md embed route's mutation boundary.\\n2. Read the agents-md engine's copy handling and the check's A1 install-state and A10 runtime-copy rows.\\n3. Read the symlink manifest's `CLAUDE.md` row and the two read-only hook checks.\\n4. Read `/doctor:setup`'s six legs and the doctor route table, and compared them with where `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` are actually called.\\n5. Re-read the after-arm delivery numbers for Claude and Codex against those install shapes.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The install offers two instruction-file shapes with opposite outcomes for Claude Code: `link` makes `CLAUDE.md` a symlink to the checkout's `AGENTS.md`, while `embed` folds a project `CLAUDE.md` into `AGENTS.md` and removes it, leaving no file named `CLAUDE.md` in the project. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json:23] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:29]\\n\\n2. The agents-md check is asymmetric. It has a named `claude-only` install state for a repository with `CLAUDE.md` and no `AGENTS.md`, but no state or row for the reverse shape that `embed` produces. A10 accepts `absent` as an expected `CLAUDE.md`, so an embed install with no Claude instruction file passes the check. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:217] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:738]\\n\\n3. The install's final step is not truthful about brief delivery. `/doctor:setup` runs six read-only legs, and none of them reports whether a runtime received a brief or whether its prompt hook is approved; the Codex approval check runs only under `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, and the hook-wiring check only under `/doctor:symlink check`. A fresh Codex install can therefore print `STATUS=OK` with 0 of 24 briefs delivered. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:54] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:41] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60]\\n\\n4. The measured after arm lands exactly on those two shapes: Codex delivered 0 of 24 briefs because a fresh checkout's project hooks are unapproved, and Claude delivered 24 of 24 briefs but 0 of 24 Gate 2 bullets because the arena had no project `CLAUDE.md` and the global file points at the main checkout. Two of six runtimes reach a nominally successful install with either no brief or no policy definition. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:130] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:135]\\n\\n5. The cheap repair fits both readings of Claude's instruction loading: a one-line `@AGENTS.md` pointer is not a copy, so it cannot double-load or drift, and the manifest's own expected set already lists `pointer` for `CLAUDE.md`. No validator change is needed; only the engine's default and the check's missing row. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:738]\\n\\n6. The install guide does not tell the person what the instruction-file choice costs per runtime. Step 1 says `embed` \\\"adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`\\\" and step 2 repeats it; neither says `embed` removes `CLAUDE.md`, and neither names Claude as the runtime that depends on it. [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:133] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:146]\\n\\n7. Both repairs are display and file-authoring changes with no process and no scorer path: one 12-byte pointer written at embed time, one check row that reads the project `CLAUDE.md`, and one `/doctor:setup` line that calls the two existing read-only checks. [INFERENCE: based on the embed engine's allowlist and the setup legs' read-only invariant]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Write the operator's global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` from the install path: outside the repository, declared report-only by the manifest, and it changes what every session on the machine loads. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:777]\\n- Keep a full `CLAUDE.md` copy from `embed`: the manifest's own reason says a full copy double-loads or drifts; a pointer avoids both. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:744]\\n- Leave the Codex signal to `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`: a person who ran the six printed install steps has no reason to run a seventh command, so the zero stays silent. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:54]\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a setup leg that already covers brief delivery: the advisor leg checks `advisor_status` freshness, not a delivered brief, and the embedder leg checks the semantic lane. Neither reads a run log or a hook approval. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:57]\\n- Looking for a check that fails on the embed shape: A1 only names `claude-only`, and A10 accepts `absent`, so both rows pass. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:217]\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"external repository setup\\\" could mean the link engine, the instruction file or the hook approval. All three are on the printed install path, so all three were measured; the instruction file is the one with a runtime-specific zero.\\n- Contradictory evidence: carried from iteration 1 between the manifest's \\\"Claude reads the root document directly\\\" and the measured arena. The pointer recommendation is deliberately valid under both.\\n- Missing dependencies: none; all reads were local and no command wrote outside the lineage.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.72\\n- Questions addressed: KQ3\\n- Questions answered: KQ3\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: following the printed install steps in order, then asking what each final check actually reads, found a green status that no measured runtime supports. Comparing the two instruction-file shapes explained why the same brief behaved differently on Claude between the main checkout and the arena.\\n- What did not work and why: searching for an existing brief-delivery leg failed because every leg is a component check; none composes \\\"the runtime can receive a brief\\\" from the hook file plus the approval plus the instruction file.\\n- What I would do differently: start from the final status line and walk backwards; the misleading green is the finding, and the file shapes are its cause.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nKQ4 and KQ5: the embedder keep-alive decision with its memory and latency numbers, then the ranking. The install-side findings already supply two of the ranked items; the ranking needs the cost side measured before it can order them.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540232540,"end":1794540250731}}}}
