{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540509299,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2f30e97001bnAgJo1m7lmSBh","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc364ffeqbG9co4b48ZLH6","messageID":"msg_1d2f2e1f5001l6ZCWZoYmXs71z","type":"tool","id":"call_aefc5d3c74904bdab0d6bee7","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md","oldString":"## Recommended Next Focus\n\nKQ3: the external-repository install path.","newString":"## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n\nTwo workflow steps that would write outside this lineage were skipped, not executed, under the dispatch's write limit:\n\n- `phase_init.step_preinit_spec_branch` classifies `spec-present` and would append the research topic to `{spec_folder}/spec.md` under Open Questions and Research Context. The file was read for classification and left unchanged.\n- `phase_synthesis.step_writeback_spec_findings` and `step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc` would replace a generated findings fence in `spec.md` and run `validate.sh` on the parent packet. Both are parent-packet writes; the lineage records the conflict here and stops at its own synthesis.\n- `phase_save` (`generate-context.js`) was not run: the dispatch bans it, and the lineage's completion is its own artifacts.\n\nNo file outside the lineage was created, modified or deleted.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nKQ3: the external-repository install path."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md\n@@ -70,7 +70,17 @@\n - What worked and why: computing the brief from the renderer and the generated table, rather than trusting the reported 242-298 bytes, exposed that the head is only 27% of the brief and that the constant block never shrinks. Parsing the table also made the \"room for a gloss\" question numeric instead of rhetorical.\n - What did not work and why: looking for an emitter-side suppression failed because the state machine is a measurement surface; segment one read its own shadow metric as delivery.\n - What I would do differently: read the returned string before the shadow log next time; the emitted bytes are the only cost that reaches the model.\n \n+## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n+\n+Two workflow steps that would write outside this lineage were skipped, not executed, under the dispatch's write limit:\n+\n+- `phase_init.step_preinit_spec_branch` classifies `spec-present` and would append the research topic to `{spec_folder}/spec.md` under Open Questions and Research Context. The file was read for classification and left unchanged.\n+- `phase_synthesis.step_writeback_spec_findings` and `step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc` would replace a generated findings fence in `spec.md` and run `validate.sh` on the parent packet. Both are parent-packet writes; the lineage records the conflict here and stops at its own synthesis.\n+- `phase_save` (`generate-context.js`) was not run: the dispatch bans it, and the lineage's completion is its own artifacts.\n+\n+No file outside the lineage was created, modified or deleted.\n+\n ## Recommended Next Focus\n \n KQ3: the external-repository install path. The embed branch removes the project `CLAUDE.md` that the Claude Code path needs, and the install's final `/doctor:setup` does not report whether any brief was delivered, so a fresh install can finish green with a runtime at zero.\n","status":"modified","additions":10,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-cost-2/iterations/iteration-001.md\",\"oldString\":\"## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nKQ3: the external-repository install path.\",\"newString\":\"## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\\n\\nTwo workflow steps that would write outside this lineage were skipped, not executed, under the dispatch's write limit:\\n\\n- `phase_init.step_preinit_spec_branch` classifies `spec-present` and would append the research topic to `{spec_folder}/spec.md` under Open Questions and Research Context. The file was read for classification and left unchanged.\\n- `phase_synthesis.step_writeback_spec_findings` and `step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc` would replace a generated findings fence in `spec.md` and run `validate.sh` on the parent packet. Both are parent-packet writes; the lineage records the conflict here and stops at its own synthesis.\\n- `phase_save` (`generate-context.js`) was not run: the dispatch bans it, and the lineage's completion is its own artifacts.\\n\\nNo file outside the lineage was created, modified or deleted.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nKQ3: the external-repository install path.\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540506775,"end":1794540509299}}}}
